    "reasoning": "All ten mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-62051: the prism has two square faces of area 4 and four rectangular faces of area 6, giving 2(4)+4(6)=32 ft². q-62256: the square base has area 4 and each triangular face has area (1/2)(2)(9)=9, giving 4+4(9)=40 m²; the stated 9 m is the side-face height. q-99275: a positive multiple of x^12 tends to positive infinity as x tends to positive infinity. q-35243: f(x) tends to 3, so its reciprocal tends to the positive number 1/3 while x² grows without bound; the quotient tends to positive infinity. q-35192: x^5 tends to negative infinity, and multiplication by -1/4 reverses the sign. q-35379: the negative leading term -x^4 dominates the constant, giving negative infinity. q-1856: differentiating 2x^-2-3x^(3/4) gives -4x^-3-(9/4)x^-1/4. q-102192: differentiating (1/3)x^-3/2 gives -(1/2)x^-5/2, equivalent to the supplied radical form for x>0. q-1804 and q-6529: ordering distinct objects gives 5!=120 and 10!=3,628,800, respectively. No prior submitted answer or grade is supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
